{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban the sale and use of fireworks to the general public",
        "additional_details": "Far too many animals both domesticated or those that live outside are scared or hurt by the noise of fireworks. Fireworks should be restricted to licence holders only and should only be used on 5th November or within agreed government dates close to that date and then on New Year\u2019s Eve. We believe far too many people are setting fireworks off days or weeks before November 5th which simply prolongs the cruelty to animals. With a law that restricts the sales and use of fireworks and which has stated dates, we can help the animals more.",
        "background": "Ban sales of fireworks to the general public and restrict their sale and use to those having licences for displays only. Far too many animals are scared by fireworks which isn\u2019t fair on them. They can also hurt people when others bust and use them irresponsibly.",
